ces 142 violations and 114 parity issues. Native annular geometry violates the saved 0.10 mm constraint despite explicit exclusions. Zero unconnected items does not satisfy the separate DRC criterion; excluded thermal errors alone do not prove opens.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"duplicate_of\": null,\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"locator\": \"Symbol d69380f9-5487-4782-9ce9-0690df62e543: value 120, dnp yes; instances R36/R37\",\n          \"path\": \"inputs/project/wbo-can-trans.kicad_sch\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"locator\": \"components.R36/R37; nets /CAN2+ and /CAN2-, including J2.73/74 and J1.15/11\",\n          \"path\": \"work/netlist/connectivity.json\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"locator\": \"can2.resistors; can2.direct_resistors; populated_carrier_direct_conductance_S=0\",\n          \"path\": \"review-work/adjudicator/experiments/audit.json\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"finding_id\": \"circuit/circuit-can2-termination\",\n      \"reason\": \"The carrier has no populated direct resistive termination, but attached module/harness termination and operating topology are unestablished. Communication failure is therefore unproven. Preserve this major uncertainty pending intended external circuitry and assembled-bus termination/topology evidence; no carrier-local termination requirement is declared.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"disposition\": \"duplicate\",\n      \"duplicate_of\": \"check/erc\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"locator\": \"sheets[0].violations[0–4]\",\n          \"path\": \"work/erc/erc.json\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"locator\": \"erc.identical_records.sheets=true; native_erc_declarations\",\n          \"path\": \"review-work/adjudicator/experiments/audit.json\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"finding_id\": \"circuit/circuit-erc-declarations\",\n      \"reason\": \"These are the same five established declaration errors retained under the accepted ERC finding.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"disposition\": \"accepted\",\n      \"duplicate_of\": null,\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"locator\": \"Lines 21687–21725: five unnumbered thru_hole pads with size equal to drill\",\n          \"path\": \"inputs/project/Polygonus-Universal-Base.kicad_pcb\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"locator\": \"violations[137–141]: minimum annular width 0.1000 mm; actual 0.0000 mm\",\n          \"path\": \"work/drc/drc.json\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"locator\": \"holes: all five annulus_mm=0; annular_rule_mm=0.1\",\n          \"path\": \"review-work/adjudicator/experiments/audit.json\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"locator\": \"Plated tools T10: two 2.200 mm holes; T12: three 4.000 mm holes\",\n          \"path\": \"review-work/adjudicator/experiments/drill-report.txt\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"finding_id\": \"physical/physical-001\",\n      \"reason\": \"Native geometry and independent drill export establish five plated holes with zero nominal annular land, violating the saved 0.10 mm constraint. Exclusions do not alter the geometry. This establishes a manufacturing-data defect without proving connector misfit or fabrication impossibility.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"disposition\": \"duplicate\",\n      \"duplicate_of\": \"circuit/circuit-can2-termination\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"locator\": \"components.R36/R37.dnp=true; nets /CAN2+ and /CAN2-\",\n          \"path\": \"work/netlist/connectivity.json\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"locator\": \"can2.resistors and populated_carrier_direct_conductance_S\",\n          \"path\": \"review-work/adjudicator/experiments/audit.json\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"finding_id\": \"physical/physical-002\",\n      \"reason\": \"Same omitted carrier termination and unresolved external-hardware condition as the canonical deferred CAN2 concern; no separate failure mechanism is established.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"run_id\": \"c91cb6bf-3f83-487a-88